{
  "title": "Projectile Target Challenge: Pick Angle and Speed",
  "description": "A launcher sits at the left end of a flat 70 m green field with distance marks every 10 m. A red target disc with a flag sits down the field. Set the launch angle and speed, then press Launch: the ball flies its arc and leaves a trail. Your previous arc stays as a faded line. The readouts show the landing distance, how far you missed, and whether the shot was short or long. Hit targets at 30 m, 45 m and 18 m using no more than 10 launches.",
  "experience": "game",
  "behavior": "rules",
  "controlProfile": "inspect",
  "stepped": true,
  "game": {
    "objective": "Hit 3 targets (30 m, 45 m, then 18 m) using no more than 10 launches. A hit lands within 1.5 m of the target centre.",
    "hint": "At the same speed, angles that add up to 90° (like 30° and 60°) land at the same distance, and 45° goes farthest. Doubling the speed makes the shot go four times as far."
  },
