  "assumptions": [
    "This is a simplified simulation: no air resistance, and the ball starts at ground level on flat ground.",
    "Gravity is 9.8 m/s² straight down. The sideways speed stays constant and only the vertical speed changes.",
    "Each step is computed exactly from the projectile formulas, so the landing distance equals speed² × sin(2 × angle) ÷ 9.8.",
    "The ball is a point in the physics; it is drawn large (1.5 m radius) so you can see it, and its centre is drawn 1.5 m above the computed point so it rests on the ground.",
    "A hit is a landing within 1.5 m of the target centre, counting both edges. The red disc shows that zone. Real balls are slowed by air and would land shorter.",
    "Each flight is shown over about two seconds, whatever its real flight time. Targets come in a fixed order, so Reset starts the same challenge with score and trails cleared."
  ],
